--[[
    Blueprint Manager (In-Game)  --  v5
    Run as a LocalScript in StarterPlayerScripts.

    UNIVERSAL PLACEMENT CONTRACT
    ----------------------------
    The remote places the model so its pivot lands exactly at
    RelativeCFrame (relative to the reference part), then applies
    OriginalOffset internally for resize anchoring.

    Therefore:
      * Export writes  relativeCFrame = reference:ToObjectSpace(pivot)
        verbatim. No bbox-bottom substitution, no surface anchoring,
        no per-id branching.
      * Import sends that same CFrame verbatim. No subtraction of
        OriginalOffset.
      * offsetCFrame is stored in the blueprint ONLY for dupe-key
        differentiation, never applied to placement.

    PlacementSurface / Surface_Default is recorded in the diagnostic
    output for reference only. It is descriptive metadata about where
    the pivot sits relative to the model's bbox (e.g. "Back" for
    wall-mounted items whose pivot is above the bbox bottom); it does
    NOT change placement. The remote anchors on the pivot, full stop.

    Debug:
        Scan Target    -- deep-diagnose first 50 models
        Deep Scan All  -- deep-diagnose all (capped at 300)
        Diff Templates -- one summary line per distinct id
]]

